<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Friends' But Who Benefits? Notes from an Historic Summit, Myanmar's Genocide Ruling, Time to 'Bre-join' the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9748ceaa66ec81dd673e75b5805b7c44a3cad5a70d78bf4fe02564fc859a4d4a</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:27:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T19:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261120-friends-but-who-benefits-notes-from-an-historic-summit-myanmar-s-genocide-ruling-time-to-br--18c7cf7590a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261120-friends-but-who-benefits-notes-from-an-historic-summit-myanmar-s-genocide-ruling-time-to-bre-join-the-eu" /><summary type="html">Welcome to the World This Week with Gavin Lee. You give us 45 minutes, we'll give you 7 days worth of crystal clear analysis. As ever, alongside a handpicked panel of four distinguished foreign correspondents.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Shenzhen trilateral: Xi Jinping's 'masterclass in diplomatic theatre'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c70731806e39635fc69a3c9943b1d9ffbc08ef3cd9cd04a238147d3264af414</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T15:37:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261120-shenzhen-trilateral-xi-jinping-s-masterclass-in-diplomatic-theatre--3189c813d399.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20261120-shenzhen-trilateral-xi-jinping-s-masterclass-in-diplomatic-theatre" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping positioned himself as a great statesman when he met with the US president and Russia's Vladimir Putin for trilateral talks in Shenzhen this week. But while the Chinese president sparkled on the world stage, does he have anything to show for it? Seong-Hyon Lee, an associate at Harvard University Asia Center, tells us how the trilateral has come up short on deliverables.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Malaysia's unwanted refugees: The plight of the Rohingya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e21bfe2ef2e86707ee6d1973e7c684a86a73f300fe311f25626478493fd30a32</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T11:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya--4971af38a2e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya" /><summary type="html">On November 19, the International Court of Justice delivered a historic ruling: finding Myanmar guilty of committing genocide against the Rohingya in 2017. Malaysia has long been a supporter of the persecuted Muslim minority. But its role as a safe haven is coming to an end, amid a rise in hate speech and calls for the expulsion of Rohingya via social media.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Was the historic Shenzhen summit a political win or humiliation for Putin?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7993777f35be69c74c801ad607b444132f3f2c38442b0e5275cfec8b81c7624b</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T10:42:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261120-was-the-historic-shenzhen-summit-political-win-or-humiliation-for-putin--15f69b1b64a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261120-was-the-historic-shenzhen-summit-political-win-or-humiliation-for-putin" /><summary type="html">The world watched with bated breath Thursday as the presidents of China, Russia and the United States met for 90 minutes for an unprecedented trilateral summit in Shenzhen. Each leader came to the negotiating table with their own motivations. But Russia's Vladimir Putin was seen as walking away worse off than his counterparts, with some media outlets reporting the Kremlin leader was "humiliated" during the talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Xi-Trump-Putin trilateral meeting: Trump's recognition of China and Russia as 'peers of the US'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52dd1e7f7ff561214c63486f0023db9b51c870e51180df76e0699a740522244d</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:33:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/xi-trump-putin-trilateral-meeting-trump-s-recognition-of-china-and-russia-as-peers-of-the-us--44673d48958c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/xi-trump-putin-trilateral-meeting-trump-s-recognition-of-china-and-russia-as-peers-of-the-us" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Olivia Cheung. The trilateral meeting between Donald Trump, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin at the APEC summit was significant despite the absence of concrete agreements, according to Cheung. “The significance is seen in the precedence of the United States seeing and giving recognition that China and Russia are peers of the United States,” she explained, adding that “the image of a G3 is very significant.”</summary></entry><entry><title>What impact will the Shenzhen summit have on the US-China trade war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5afe90836a7b62bb7387ebb7121f283cab4948a623de149569391307e3729fd9</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T17:34:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-what-impact-will-shenzhen-summit-us-china-trade-war--96c2486832f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-what-impact-will-shenzhen-summit-us-china-trade-war" /><summary type="html">Despite warm words between US President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping at three-way talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Shenzhen Thursday, the simmering trade war between Washington and Beijing still looks to be no closer to resolution.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Bangladesh: Hasina supporters vandalise ruling party office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aedfa5b143f823827176d8964ecc3bd4a743f7733dda1afe75d04eb1fe161c53</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T17:14:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-bangladesh-hasina-supporters-vandalise-ruling-party-office--4e2388b723df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-bangladesh-hasina-supporters-vandalise-ruling-party-office" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of supporters of ousted Bangladesh premier Sheikh Hasina staged street protests on Thursday, as a wave of arson attacks escalated tensions ahead of her planned return from exile next month.</summary></entry><entry><title>ICJ ruling on Myanmar genocide: ‘Historic victory for Rohingya, landmark for international justice’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78e35cff6e8610e1c45ce3fe6d2227e930588e6e9606aaeed078895afe0be3a0</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:54:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/icj-ruling-on-myanmar-genocide-historic-victory-for-rohingya-landmark-for-international-justice--384182b693e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/icj-ruling-on-myanmar-genocide-historic-victory-for-rohingya-landmark-for-international-justice" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye welcomes Reed Brody, Member of the International Commission of Jurists, Human Rights Lawyer and veteran war crimes prosecutor. The International Court of Justice's ruling on Myanmar marks, according to Brody, "a historic victory for the Rohingya, but also a landmark for international justice." He explains how the court assessed evidence of genocidal intent, rejecting Myanmar's justification of its military operations as counterterrorism. He argues that "the existence of an armed conflict or a security objective doesn't exclude genocidal intent," a finding he believes will have "far-reaching implications in future genocide cases," including South Africa's case against Israel over Gaza. Brody also discusses the Gambia's role in bringing the case and growing challenges to international accountability, warning that "we're in a very dangerous moment."</summary></entry><entry><title>Xi demonstrating China's 'global status', occupying 'central position' in relation to Trump &amp; Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b77ad8a82d512d53d29377766ad426035a479ffa6f066dd612ae425f15692d6d</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:40:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/xi-demonstrating-china-s-global-status-occupying-central-position-in-relation-to-trump-putin--9ea64aca799a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/xi-demonstrating-china-s-global-status-occupying-central-position-in-relation-to-trump-putin" /><summary type="html">Sharon Gaffney is pleased to welcome Rex Li, professor of international relations at King's College London. For Professor Li, the meeting between Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin in China is less about "reaching concrete agreements and a common position." Rather, he argues, it is about demonstrating Xi's ability to bring the American and Russian leaders together to discuss major geopolitical issues. Li believes that Xi Jinping has the most to gain from the meeting, as it allows him to demonstrate China's global status and its role as a diplomatic convener. Putin may also benefit from the opportunity to meet the two leaders despite Russia's international isolation following its invasion of Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>ICJ rules Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5bef93244b4b1390ce530b405256dbff072612b073efa9b63861b63fc88ca724</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:07:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/icj-rules-myanmar-committed-genocide-against-the-rohingya--76a6ec8c41e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/icj-rules-myanmar-committed-genocide-against-the-rohingya" /><summary type="html">In August 2017, after attacks by a Rohingya militia, Myanmar’s army launched a “clearance campaign” in Rakhine state, with survivors describing mass killings, rapes and burned villages as hundreds of thousands fled to Bangladesh. The Gambia took Myanmar to the ICJ in 2019, and after a seven-year legal fight the court has ruled that Myanmar committed acts of genocide. Meanwhile some 1.2 million Rohingya remain in crowded camps, unable to return home.</summary></entry><entry><title>China summit ends with little new, Europe backs Ukraine in Berlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80a22d619b4356557886f82de8c81e74b2d3c8a425e06cdef38bd8c41122d14f</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T14:04:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin--41fb764541d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/china-summit-ends-with-little-new-europe-backs-ukraine-in-berlin" /><summary type="html">The leaders of China, the United States and Russia met in Shenzhen for a historic first, but the summit brought little new: non-binding statements on peace and no plan to meet regularly. In Berlin, Europeans gathered to show their support for Ukraine, a pointed answer to a summit where Europe had no seat, as FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>In South Korea, women forced into prostitution on US military bases seek justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21848bf81979ca48860ad8306b0195382ec614788b0979e3039ba377a334f715</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:21:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261119-in-south-korea-women-forced-into-prostitution-on-us-military-bases-seek-justice--69f7c325b834.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261119-in-south-korea-women-forced-into-prostitution-on-us-military-bases-seek-justice" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of women were forced to work in South Korean state-sanctioned brothels used by American soldiers based in the country after the Korean War. They were raped, physically abused and forcibly confined. Now, after decades of silence, some of these women are speaking out.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>'Their lives, their rights, their history': Not the end of accountability for the Rohingya people'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5082853147323a7047fe79c975c072ac22f10f89817f1de625ecb8603152832c</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:19:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/their-lives-their-rights-their-history-not-the-end-of-accountability-for-the-rohingya-people--d94c339abf0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/their-lives-their-rights-their-history-not-the-end-of-accountability-for-the-rohingya-people" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry welcomes Sonya Sceats, Director and CEO of the British Institute of International and Comparative Law. The case brought by The Gambia against Myanmar before the ICJ, and the court ruling, both have great significance for the Rohingya people, the interpretation of the Genocide Convention and the possibility of future criminal proceedings. The case could also have important implications for South Africa's proceedings against Israel, where there are “many similarities between the two cases.”</summary></entry><entry><title>What to know about Xi, Putin and Trump's historic trilateral summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71d5e31e5ff9a31f0587d454ed72e229487074868162a85a7f587a61493376a3</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:11:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-what-to-know-about-xi-putin-and-trump-s-historic-trilateral-summit--252930a78203.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-what-to-know-about-xi-putin-and-trump-s-historic-trilateral-summit" /><summary type="html">China's Xi Jinping, Russian President Vladimir Putin and his US counterpart Donald Trump met for a historic summit in Shenzhen, China, on Thursday, where they agreed on a "peace declaration". The three leaders pledged to reform the UN, increase supplies of refined petroleum products and uphold the immunity enjoyed by officials in international courts.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Myanmar's Rohingya case: how does the ICJ define genocide?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bea98411958a1da834bf4de2fc3ac034f1b75f58caaa25d746eb549c2994710</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T11:22:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/myanmar-s-rohingya-case-how-does-the-icj-define-genocide--783277d01e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/myanmar-s-rohingya-case-how-does-the-icj-define-genocide" /><summary type="html">The ICJ is preparing to rule on whether Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya, in a case brought by The Gambia after the 2017 crackdown. The key legal test is proving intent to destroy a group, which is notoriously hard, and the court’s reading of it could also weigh on South Africa’s case against Israel.</summary></entry><entry><title>'We are making history,' says Trump at historic trilateral with Xi and Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:201b71297f7308ac6858316ce550d11f3058513c456383c345c29428ccf2a2a4</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T11:02:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-we-are-making-history-says-trump-at-historic-trilateral-with-xi-and-putin--b8d6e37eaab2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-we-are-making-history-says-trump-at-historic-trilateral-with-xi-and-putin" /><summary type="html">The first meeting in history between US, Chinese and Russian leaders has kicked off in Shenzhen, China. "We are really making history," said the US president to his counterparts.</summary></entry><entry><title>APEC Summit: Lots of gloss, little real progress?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:585eea84cf4cf9ce7dc998e5cc4991a274c897b8755fa90f674f49d06fb83582</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:47:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/apec-summit-lots-of-gloss-little-real-progress--a38d68b281eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/apec-summit-lots-of-gloss-little-real-progress" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin are holding their first-ever trilateral meeting in Shenzhen, on the sidelines of the APEC forum. It is a historic moment in more ways than one, with the leaders of the world’s three most powerful countries around the same table. Ukraine, the war in Iran, nuclear disarmament and artificial intelligence are all expected to be discussed, and the summit has stoked fears of a carve-up of the world into spheres of influence. But despite the buzz, analysts expect more symbolism than substance, with few concrete breakthroughs likely. Our correspondent in the region has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Xi, Trump, Putin: historic summit ends, outcome unclear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfc0e8bbf6341763a27f778fc77031cf0d5a614737d241713aeab6a682f78732</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:42:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/xi-trump-putin-historic-summit-ends-outcome-unclear--4f099cb3964b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/xi-trump-putin-historic-summit-ends-outcome-unclear" /><summary type="html">The unprecedented trilateral summit between Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin ended on Thursday in Shenzhen after about an hour and 20 minutes. No details have emerged yet, but the three leaders talking face to face is already an event. Each has their own agenda: Putin wants to be back on the world stage, Trump needs a win at home, and Xi is asserting China’s status as an economic superpower. What comes out of it remains unclear, as FRANCE 24's journalists explain.</summary></entry><entry><title>APEC Summit: Trump, Putin, Xi hold 'historic' meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10ade7c0c47c6b125c855b9d507b93be9c7bd28232c0302a0468b0e4409875ac</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T10:19:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-apec-summit-trump-putin-xi-hold-historic-meeting--3ef03f7311ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261119-apec-summit-trump-putin-xi-hold-historic-meeting" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 🇷🇺 US President Donald #Trump, Russia's Vladimir #Putin and Chinese leader #Xi Jinping kicked off their first trilateral talks in Shenzhen. 
 
Beijing said the meeting is aimed at "safeguarding world peace", but it has raised fears of a carve up of the globe into "spheres of influence".</summary></entry><entry><title>Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin begin unprecedented summit in China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51f58c57e3716ae331e43748b0ce4693244c4f59594d1a44692ef6aac9fa721</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T09:07:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-begin-unprecedented-summit-in-china--82bb7bc072ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/xi-jinping-donald-trump-and-vladimir-putin-begin-unprecedented-summit-in-china" /><summary type="html">Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin opened their first trilateral talks in Shenzhen on the sidelines of the APEC forum, a meeting analysts expect to offer more symbolism than breakthroughs and that critics fear could carve the world into spheres of influence. Ukraine, the Iran war, nuclear disarmament and AI are all expected to come up, while Trump and Xi also held one-on-one talks on trade and technology.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Korea tightens security for national exam over AI cheating scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b19df869d453bdfc21f80dcdde5577e1ec21a4715d89511291855421d1b9fa5</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T08:55:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-korea-tightens-security-for-national-exam-over-ai-cheating-scandal--f5a3204bc312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-korea-tightens-security-for-national-exam-over-ai-cheating-scandal" /><summary type="html">More than 550,000 candidates sat South Korea’s Suneung university entrance exam under extraordinary security, after an AI cheating scandal in which a top scorer on a national tax accountant exam admitted using a hidden mini camera to send questions to an AI system. Authorities inspected students’ glasses, deployed thousands of extra supervisors and ordered stickers over every button on candidates’ clothing. A nationwide disaster alert was also sent to make even muted phones buzz, exposing any devices smuggled into exam rooms.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nuclear arms at the center of the Shenzhen trilateral meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b36967accec4fdc37fefca6ccc74a259d4f5a71226292741163b83a1d32d272b</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T08:36:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nuclear-arms-at-the-center-of-the-schenzhen-trilateral-meeting--cd3b3ca72551.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nuclear-arms-at-the-center-of-the-schenzhen-trilateral-meeting" /><summary type="html">Nuclear weapons are at the top of Donald Trump’s agenda at the trilateral summit in Beijing. The US president wants the United States, Russia and China to reduce their nuclear stockpiles, and FRANCE 24’s Philip Turle expects him to push hard for a three-way agreement on the issue. Iran is also a key part of the discussion. The three leaders share an interest in preventing the Iranian regime from acquiring nuclear weapons. Regional conflicts and oil prices are also se to be central issues.</summary></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: AI and tech competition between US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5d4beceb9cfa78277e149e7e40a7d9a6f9be1d37e1abf667473e50ad193fee8</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T07:45:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-summit-ai-and-tech-competition-between-us-and-china--e658ecbd7880.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-summit-ai-and-tech-competition-between-us-and-china" /><summary type="html">Chinese President Xi Jinping is welcoming US President Donald Trump and Russia’s Vladimir Putin on Thursday for the first-ever three-way summit between the leaders. Beyond the wars in Ukraine and Iran, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies are expected to feature in the talks between Washington and Beijing, as the two powers compete for the lead in AI, advanced chips and other strategic technologies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Myanmar committed genocide against Muslim Rohingya minority, UN court finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20771907edc121e1dd1ec68b4ea006793fcf264a8258c479e799057c8f792b7a</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T03:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-top-un-court-to-rule-if-myanmar-s-rohingya-crackdown-was-genocide--476d74703607.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-top-un-court-to-rule-if-myanmar-s-rohingya-crackdown-was-genocide" /><summary type="html">The United Nations International Court of Justice on Thursday ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against its Muslim Rohingya minority. It is the ⁠first time a state ​has been ‌found responsible for genocide at the ‌court.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Xi and Putin agree a nuclear war 'must never be fought' at landmark meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4156de9bcec70bc72350da672d5f7379c157804d25929db414032ad59cc30121</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T01:47:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-xi-trump-putin-talks-live-china-us-russia-leaders-hold-landmark-three-way-meeting--0e21cc420896.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261119-xi-trump-putin-talks-live-china-us-russia-leaders-hold-landmark-three-way-meeting" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump, China's Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin agreed on Thursday at a historic trilateral summit in Shenzhen, China, that a "nuclear war cannot be won and must never be fought". Read our blog to see how the three-way talks unfolded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Xi welcomes Trump: Does Nvidia scandal upend US-China AI race?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8828a395c998e3e71106146abaee70358a5cab29a0734a2cfde57e9c0aad6451</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T19:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261118-xi-welcomes-trump-does-nvidia-scandal-upend-us-china-ai-race--9efab38c66c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261118-xi-welcomes-trump-does-nvidia-scandal-upend-us-china-ai-race" /><summary type="html">You can strike Jensen Huang from the guest list, but good luck steering dinner conversation away from the topic in Shenzhen. The co-founder of the AI computing giant was set to accompany the US president to the APEC summit before he was undone by revelations of a dalliance with a Chinese national that happened to coincide with a Singapore client's backdoor skirting of sanctions on its powerful H200 chips.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing has supported Moscow but 'China understands that America is way more important than Russia'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45902bc58f05b37e8381c889a5da265c4707f5948ab2f35fe472dab579203e5f</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T17:48:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia--f9f88efc8e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/beijing-has-supported-moscow-but-china-understands-that-america-is-way-more-important-than-russia" /><summary type="html">Following Xi Jinping's very friendly rare tarmac greeting for Donald Trump, Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Kerry Brown, Professor of Chinese Studies and Director of the Lau China Institute at King's College, London. Brown examines the complex relationship between the world's two largest economies, China's growing diplomatic influence and the competition over artificial intelligence.“China is the diplomatic center of the world,” says Brown, pointing to Beijing's ability to bring together leaders from Russia, the United States, Europe and elsewhere. He argues that China now has “extraordinary convening power" and significant influence over Russia.</summary></entry><entry><title>Three leaders, three agendas: Who wants what from Xi-Trump-Putin summit?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a3034082f7e5c2109d1e37649c1810a6a9b8e60670041ae53d6e31015438b4e</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:52:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-three-leaders-three-agendas-who-wants-what-from-xi-trump-putin-summit--77d1e7e2147c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-three-leaders-three-agendas-who-wants-what-from-xi-trump-putin-summit" /><summary type="html">Be it curbing arms sales to Taiwan, bouncing back after a midterms shellacking, or the optics of a place at the table with the world's two superpowers, Xi Jinping, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin are approaching their trilateral meeting in Shenzhen with starkly different aims and agendas. Here's a look at what the Chinese, US and Russian leaders are hoping for.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea completes external works on enrichment facility extension, says IAEA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53178fff69f945c79af904a2a313487907fcfdf4a99261583e604ade8c092a1f</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T13:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-north-korea-completes-external-works-on-enrichment-facility-extension-says-iaea--1279187574c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261118-north-korea-completes-external-works-on-enrichment-facility-extension-says-iaea" /><summary type="html">A new extension to North Korea's Yongbyon enrichment facility has been "externally complete" since mid-October, according to the International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), which relies on satellite imagery and open sources to monitor the country's nuclear programme. IAEA chief Rafael Grossi on Wednesday said expansion of Pyongyang's enrichment programme remains "cause for serious concern".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Trump arrives in China ahead of trilateral summit with Putin and Xi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b566587ac7e763644ce662ee915f0ca149b48e3f4286a3bb95cec59687a561e</id><updated>2026-11-21T07:26:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T11:46:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-trump-arrives-in-china-ahead-of-trilateral-summit-with-putin-and-xi--e1f90483e436.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261118-trump-arrives-in-china-ahead-of-trilateral-summit-with-putin-and-xi" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump arrived in Shenzhen, China on Wednesday, ahead of a historic trilateral on the sidelines of the APEC summit with his Russian and Chinese counterparts. The three men are expected to address the wars in Ukraine and Iran as well as nuclear disarmament.</summary></entry></feed>
